{
  "id": "32277_kaeru",
  "headword": "{孵|かえ}る",
  "reading": "かえる",
  "romaji": "kaeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to hatch",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to hatch",
      "explanation": "For an egg to hatch, or for a chick or other young animal to come out of its egg. The subject can be the egg or the young."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "32277_kaeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{卵|たまご}→卵：02222_tamago⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{孵|かえ}った。",
      "english": "The egg hatched.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "32277_kaeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "ひな⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{孵|かえ}る⟦まで→まで：00490_made⟧⟦{親鳥|おやどり}→親鳥：25490_oyadori⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦{卵|たまご}→卵：02222_tamago⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{温|あたた}める→温める：02096_atatameru⟧。",
      "english": "The parent bird keeps the eggs warm until the chicks hatch.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "32277_kaeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{三週間|さんしゅうかん}ほど⟦{温|あたた}める→温める：02096_atatameru⟧⟦と→と：00512_to⟧、⟦{鶏|にわとり}→鶏：05202_niwatori⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{卵|たまご}→卵：02222_tamago⟧⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧⟦ひよこ→ひよこ：10501_hiyoko⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{孵|かえ}る。",
      "english": "After about three weeks of incubation, chicks hatch from hen's eggs.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Usually written in hiragana (たまご⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧かえる); the kanji {孵|かえ}る is uncommon.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Pair: {孵|かえ}す (transitive — to hatch eggs, as a hen or an incubator does)\n- Pattern: ⟦{卵|たまご}→卵：02222_tamago⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{孵|かえ}る / ひな⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧かえる\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{卵|たまご}→卵：02222_tamago⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{孵|かえ}る: an egg hatches\n- ひな⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{孵|かえ}る: a chick hatches\n- ⟦{孵化|ふか}→孵化：19845_fuka⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to hatch — the formal Sino-Japanese verb used in science and news",
